--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.cond]/4: operands of the same underlying type differing in
cv-qualification or value category.  Two glvalues of the same category: the
result has the cv-combined type and keeps the category (`b ? w : cw` is an
lvalue `const W`; two xvalues give an xvalue, decltype T&&).  Different
categories: a prvalue of the cv-combined type, cv-unqualified for non-class
types ([expr.type]/2).  The shape of libstdc++'s COND-RES / common_reference.
Before, the conditional converted one operand to the other's type and yielded
a non-lvalue copy.
